@* @page "/" *@

<section class="space-y-4 rounded-xl border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Template segments</h3>
    <p class="text-sm">Segments belong to a work template. Select a template in Settings → Work Planning → Templates, then use Template Segments to add or edit its events.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Define check-in, work, breaks and check-out once. Staff schedules and generated daily plans use those definitions.</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <caption class="p-3 text-left font-medium">Example: a 16:00–22:00 template</caption>
            <thead><tr class="border-b"><th class="p-3">Segment</th><th class="p-3">Offset from start</th><th class="p-3">Expected time</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-3">Check-in</td><td class="p-3">0 minutes</td><td class="p-3">16:00</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-3">Check-out</td><td class="p-3">360 minutes</td><td class="p-3">22:00</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Each segment can specify its attendance window, grace periods and whether clocking is mandatory. Edit the template to change these rules.</p>
    <a href="/admin/work-planning/templates" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-md px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed transition-colors">Manage template segments</a>
</section>
